t><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRATORI, MAMORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, KUNIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWASAKI AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MYO NAGAYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAOKA KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIRATORI MAMORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA KUNIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWASAKI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MYO, NAGAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAOKA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRATORI, MAMORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, KUNIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A centrifugally rolling granulating and coating device (1), comprising a fixed wall (7) of which horizontal section part (7a) in contact with powder and granular material (2) is formed in circular shape and a rotating disk (5) which is installed inside the fixed wall (7) at a distance (12) and rotated horizontally by a motor (13), wherein an air feeding device (21) to feed dry air (22) to the upper surface of the rotating disk (5) is installed on the rotating disk (5), the air feeding device (21) comprises a cylindrical straight pipe part (25) and a conical air inlet port (23) and installed movably vertically in a centrifugal flow chamber (6) and, during a granulating process, the air feeding device (21) stops feeding the dry air (23), waits at an upper position (H), lowers to a lower position (L) after the granulating treating has been completed, and feeds the dry air (22) onto the rotating disk (5) to dry the granule, whereby spherical particles small in grain size, small in grain size distribution width, and high in sphericity can be produced efficiently in a single device.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à un dispositif de granulation et d'enrobage à rouleau centrifuge (1), qui comprend une paroi fixe (7) dont la section horizontale (7a) en contact avec le matériau pulvérulent et granulaire (2) est conçue sous forme circulaire, ainsi qu'un disque rotatif (5) qui est monté à l'intérieur de la paroi fixe (7) à une certaine distance (12) et mis en rotation horizontalement par un moteur (13). Un dispositif d'amenée d'air (21) introduisant de l'air sec (22) sur la surface supérieure dudit disque rotatif (5) est monté sur ledit disque rotatif (5). Ce dispositif d'amenée d'air (21) comprend un tuyau droit cylindrique (25) et un orifice d'admission d'air conique (23) et il est monté mobile à la verticale dans une chambre d'écoulement centrifuge (6) et, pendant le processus de granulation, ledit dispositif d'amenée d'air (21) interrompt l'introduction d'air sec (23), s'immobilise en attente dans une position supérieure (H), s'abaisse ensuite jusqu'à une position inférieure (L), une fois que le traitement de granulation est terminé, et introduit l'air sec (22) sur le disque rotatif (5) afin d'assécher les granules. Ainsi des particules sphériques de petite taille, ayant une faible largeur de répartition granulométrique et une sphéricité élevée peuvent être produites efficacement dans un seul dispositif.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>